package RenderingChecks

use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Model
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Models.ModelBlueprint
use Libraries.Game.Layer3D
use Libraries.Compute.Matrix4
use Libraries.Compute.Vector3

/*
Model2 is a Model that tells its TreeLayer3D when something about it
changes, so the layer does not have to look for changes every frame. It is a
test of hooks that could be added to Item3D in the standard library. It
works on any layer. On a layer other than a TreeLayer3D, it tells no one.

It reports three kinds of change:

- Moving, turning or resizing. Every action that changes its position,
  rotation or scale ends in one of the actions replaced here, including
  moves made by physics, by a parent moving its children, and by loading
  with a matrix. The model reports this once, and then not again until the
  layer has handled it, however many times it moves in between.
- Its size changing, as when a model finishes loading, so the layer can
  give it new bounds.
- Physics starting or stopping simulating it, through its
  ReportingPhysicsProperties3D, and its physics being turned on or off.

Attribute: Example

use Libraries.Game.Game
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Color
use RenderingChecks.TreeLayer3D
use RenderingChecks.Model2

class Main is Game
    action Main
        StartGame()
    end

    action CreateGame
        TreeLayer3D layer
        SetLayer(0, layer)
        SetCurrentLayer3D(layer)

        Color color
        Model2 box
        box:LoadBox(1, 1, 1, color:Teal())
        box:SetPosition(0, 0, 5)
        Add(box)
    end
end
*/
class Model2 is Model
    // True after this model has told its layer it moved, until the layer
    // has handled the move.
    boolean moveReported = false

    /*
    This action returns true if this model has reported a move its layer
    has not handled yet.

    Attribute: Returns True if a move is waiting to be handled.
    */
    action IsMoveReported returns boolean
        return moveReported
    end

    /*
    This action sets whether a move is waiting to be handled. The layer sets
    it back to false once it has handled the move.

    Attribute: Parameter value False once the move has been handled.
    */
    action SetMoveReported(boolean value)
        moveReported = value
    end

    /*
    This action moves the model sideways relative to its parent, as Model
    does, and reports the move.

    Attribute: Parameter xAmount The new offset along x.
    */
    action SetOffsetX(number xAmount)
        parent:Model:SetOffsetX(xAmount)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action moves the model up or down relative to its parent, as Model
    does, and reports the move.

    Attribute: Parameter yAmount The new offset along y.
    */
    action SetOffsetY(number yAmount)
        parent:Model:SetOffsetY(yAmount)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action moves the model forward or back relative to its parent, as
    Model does, and reports the move.

    Attribute: Parameter zAmount The new offset along z.
    */
    action SetOffsetZ(number zAmount)
        parent:Model:SetOffsetZ(zAmount)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's offset from its parent, as Model does, and
    reports the move. Every move of the model ends in this action or one of
    the three above.

    Attribute: Parameter xAmount The new offset along x.
    Attribute: Parameter yAmount The new offset along y.
    Attribute: Parameter zAmount The new offset along z.
    */
    action SetOffset(number xAmount, number yAmount, number zAmount)
        parent:Model:SetOffset(xAmount, yAmount, zAmount)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's rotation from a matrix, as Model does, and
    reports the move.

    Attribute: Parameter source The matrix to copy the rotation from.
    */
    action SetRotationTransform(Matrix4 source)
        parent:Model:SetRotationTransform(source)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action turns the model, as Model does, and reports the move. Every
    other way of turning the model goes through this action.

    Attribute: Parameter vector The axis to turn around.
    Attribute: Parameter degrees How far to turn, in degrees.
    Attribute: Parameter rotateChildren True to turn the children too.
    */
    action Rotate(Vector3 vector, number degrees, boolean rotateChildren)
        parent:Model:Rotate(vector, degrees, rotateChildren)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's rotation from angles, as Model does, and
    reports the move.

    Attribute: Parameter yaw The turn around the up direction, in degrees.
    Attribute: Parameter pitch The tilt up or down, in degrees.
    Attribute: Parameter roll The tilt to the side, in degrees.
    */
    action SetYawPitchRoll(number yaw, number pitch, number roll)
        parent:Model:SetYawPitchRoll(yaw, pitch, roll)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action scales the model, as Model does, and reports the move.
    Every other way of scaling it by an amount goes through this action.

    Attribute: Parameter vector How much to scale along each direction.
    Attribute: Parameter scaleChildren True to scale the children too.
    */
    action Scale(Vector3 vector, boolean scaleChildren)
        parent:Model:Scale(vector, scaleChildren)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's scale, as Model does, and reports the move.

    Attribute: Parameter scaleX The scale along x.
    Attribute: Parameter scaleY The scale along y.
    Attribute: Parameter scaleZ The scale along z.
    Attribute: Parameter scaleChildren True to scale the children too.
    */
    action SetScale(number scaleX, number scaleY, number scaleZ, boolean scaleChildren)
        parent:Model:SetScale(scaleX, scaleY, scaleZ, scaleChildren)
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action copies the model's physics position to what is drawn, as
    Model does, and reports the move.
    */
    action SetScreenPositionFromPhysicsPosition
        parent:Model:SetScreenPositionFromPhysicsPosition()
        ReportMove()
    end

    /*
    This action loads the model from a blueprint and places it with a
    matrix, as Model does. Every other way of loading goes through this
    action. Loading sets the model's size, which is reported by
    SetDimensions, and the matrix moves it.

    Attribute: Parameter loader The blueprint to load.
    Attribute: Parameter matrix The matrix to place the model with, or
    undefined.
    */
    action Load(ModelBlueprint loader, Matrix4 matrix)
        parent:Model:Load(loader, matrix)
        if matrix not= undefined
            ReportMove()
        end
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's width, as Model does, and reports the new
    size.

    Attribute: Parameter setWidth The new width.
    */
    action SetWidth(number setWidth)
        parent:Model:SetWidth(setWidth)
        ReportResize()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's height, as Model does, and reports the new
    size.

    Attribute: Parameter setHeight The new height.
    */
    action SetHeight(number setHeight)
        parent:Model:SetHeight(setHeight)
        ReportResize()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's depth, as Model does, and reports the new
    size.

    Attribute: Parameter setDepth The new depth.
    */
    action SetDepth(number setDepth)
        parent:Model:SetDepth(setDepth)
        ReportResize()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's width, height and depth, as Model does,
    and reports the new size.

    Attribute: Parameter setWidth The new width.
    Attribute: Parameter setHeight The new height.
    Attribute: Parameter setDepth The new depth.
    */
    action SetDimensions(number setWidth, number setHeight, number setDepth)
        parent:Model:SetDimensions(setWidth, setHeight, setDepth)
        ReportResize()
    end

    /*
    This action sets the model's width, height and depth from a vector, as
    Model does, and reports the new size. Loading a model uses this action.

    Attribute: Parameter vector The new width, height and depth.
    */
    action SetDimensions(Vector3 vector)
        parent:Model:SetDimensions(vector)
        ReportResize()
    end

    /*
    This action turns physics on or off, as Model does. When it turns
    physics on, the model's physics data is a ReportingPhysicsProperties3D,
    so the model hears when it wakes or falls asleep. Either way, the
    layer is told.

    Attribute: Parameter flag True to turn physics on.
    */
    action EnablePhysics(boolean flag)
        parent:Model:EnablePhysics(flag)
        if flag
            ReportingPhysicsProperties3D reporting
            reporting:SetItem(me)
            parent:Item3D:properties = reporting
        end

        TreeLayer3D layer = GetTreeLayer()
        if layer not= undefined
            layer:PhysicsChanged(me)
        end
    end

    /*
    This action tells the layer that physics started or stopped simulating
    this model. The model's ReportingPhysicsProperties3D calls it.
    */
    action SimulationChanged
        TreeLayer3D layer = GetTreeLayer()
        if layer not= undefined
            layer:BodySimulationChanged(me)
        end
    end

    /*
    This action tells the layer this model moved, unless it already has and
    the layer has not handled it yet.
    */
    private action ReportMove
        if moveReported
            return now
        end
        TreeLayer3D layer = GetTreeLayer()
        if layer not= undefined
            moveReported = true
            layer:ItemMoved(me)
        end
    end

    /*
    This action tells the layer this model's size changed.
    */
    private action ReportResize
        TreeLayer3D layer = GetTreeLayer()
        if layer not= undefined
            layer:ItemResized(me)
        end
    end

    /*
    This action returns this model's layer if it is a TreeLayer3D, or
    undefined otherwise.

    Attribute: Returns The layer, or undefined.
    */
    private action GetTreeLayer returns TreeLayer3D
        Layer3D layer = GetLayer()
        if layer is TreeLayer3D
            return cast(TreeLayer3D, layer)
        end
        return undefined
    end
end
